# Build-context exclusions for the ROOT (Python) image. Docker looks for
# this file in the build context root, so each context needs its own --
# see java-backend/.dockerignore and angular-frontend/.dockerignore.
#
# Audit PR-06: there was no .dockerignore anywhere, so every build shipped
# the 183 MB local dev database, the entire .git history and any local .env
# into the build context (and, for anything a COPY picked up, into an image
# layer that survives even if a later step deletes it).

# ── Never: local dev data and secrets ────────────────────────────────────
magti_portal.db
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backups/
uploads/
logs/

# ── Never: VCS and agent scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.agents
.ruff_cache

# ── Build outputs from the OTHER stacks (not part of this image) ─────────
java-backend/target/
angular-frontend/node_modules/
angular-frontend/dist/
angular-frontend/.angular/

# ── Python build noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# ── Docs and tests do not belong in a runtime image ──────────────────────
docs/
tests/
*.md
!README.md

# ── Never: destructive one-off tooling (audit 3, RTA-013) ────────────────
# These wipe whatever database DATABASE_URL points at and used to ride into
# the runtime image via `COPY . .`, one shell and one plausible-looking
# command away from erasing production. seed.py also refuses to run with
# APP_ENV=production now; keeping them out of the image is the other half,
# because a file that is not there cannot be run by mistake.
seed.py
seed_presentation_data.py
simulate_audit_data.py
scripts/seed_portal.py
scripts/seed_test_users.py
